# Agent Blueprint Protocol walkthrough

This tour reads the shipped artifacts, checks one typed denial, negotiates support, reconciles the pair, reads evidence, and runs the shipped corpus. Each notebook in the set can run on its own.

The first cell installs the published package at the release candidate requirement.

```elixir
Mix.install([{:agent_blueprint_protocol, "~> 1.0.0-rc.2"}])
```

This cell locates the installed package files and falls back to the source checkout when run from the repository.

```elixir
dependency_path =
  try do
    Mix.Project.deps_paths() |> Map.get(:agent_blueprint_protocol)
  rescue
    _ -> nil
  end

package_root =
  [dependency_path, Application.app_dir(:agent_blueprint_protocol), File.cwd!()]
  |> Enum.reject(&is_nil/1)
  |> Enum.find(fn path -> File.regular?(Path.join(path, "examples/echo-blueprint.json")) end)

true = is_binary(package_root)
%{example_files_found?: true}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{example_files_found?: true}
```

## Read the shipped examples

The package contains a Blueprint and a Deployment Manifest. Decode both and compare the Blueprint's canonical bytes with the file bytes.

Decode both shipped examples and check that the Blueprint round-trips to its original canonical bytes.

```elixir
blueprint_bytes = File.read!(Path.join(package_root, "examples/echo-blueprint.json"))
deployment_bytes = File.read!(Path.join(package_root, "examples/echo-deployment.json"))

{:ok, blueprint} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_blueprint(blueprint_bytes)
{:ok, deployment} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_deployment(deployment_bytes)
{:ok, ^blueprint_bytes} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.canonical_bytes(blueprint)

%{blueprint: true, deployment: true, canonical_round_trip: true}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{blueprint: true, deployment: true, canonical_round_trip: true}
```

## Read a typed denial

This input has an unknown top-level member. Inspect the stable error fields rather than depending on an exception.

Decode a small invalid input and keep the typed error shape.

```elixir
{:error, %AgentBlueprintProtocol.Error{} = error} =
  AgentBlueprintProtocol.decode_blueprint(~s({"unknown":true}))

%{code: error.code, subject: error.subject, detail: error.detail}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{code: :unknown_member, detail: nil, subject: []}
```

## Negotiate support

The support value lists the protocol revision accepted by this consumer. Notices are an open set, so this example matches the known name and keeps a catch-all.

Negotiate the decoded Blueprint and classify known notices while preserving a catch-all branch.

```elixir
support = %AgentBlueprintProtocol.Negotiation.Support{revisions: MapSet.new([1])}
{:ok, outcome} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.negotiate(blueprint, support)

notices =
  Enum.map(outcome.notices, fn notice ->
    case notice do
      :extension_deprecated -> :deprecated
      :extension_unknown_optional_retained -> :unknown_optional
      other -> {:unknown_notice, other}
    end
  end)

%{revision: outcome.protocol_revision, notices: notices}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{revision: 1, notices: []}
```

## Reconcile and read evidence

Reconciliation compares the artifacts with host inputs and returns protocol evidence. The summary reads every evidence field while leaving any new check shape unknown.

Call reconcile/3 with the example Deployment bounds and no supplied keys, then summarize all evidence fields.

```elixir
alias AgentBlueprintProtocol.{BoundsAlgebra, Evidence, Reconcile}

{:ok, host_bounds} = BoundsAlgebra.from_deployment(deployment)

inputs = %Reconcile.Inputs{
  host_bounds: host_bounds,
  support: support,
  keys: [],
  protected_clamp: :acknowledge,
  observations: %AgentBlueprintProtocol.Deployment.Observations{}
}

{:ok, evidence} = AgentBlueprintProtocol.reconcile(blueprint, deployment, inputs)

checks =
  Enum.map(evidence.checks, fn
    %{surface: surface, subject: subject, verified: verified, detail: detail} ->
      detail_kind =
        case detail do
          nil -> :none
          %Evidence.Binding{} -> :binding
          %Evidence.Signatures{} -> :signatures
          %BoundsAlgebra.ClampEvidence{} -> :clamp
          %AgentBlueprintProtocol.Digest{} -> :digest
          other -> {:other_detail, is_struct(other)}
        end

      {surface, subject, verified, detail_kind}

    other ->
      {:unknown_check, is_map(other)}
  end)

not_verified =
  Enum.map(evidence.not_verified, fn name ->
    case name do
      :tenancy -> :host_owned
      :live_policy -> :host_owned
      other when is_atom(other) -> :additional_surface
      _unknown -> :unknown_shape
    end
  end)

%{
  protocol_revision: evidence.protocol_revision,
  blueprint_digest: AgentBlueprintProtocol.Digest.to_tagged(evidence.blueprint_digest),
  deployment_digest: AgentBlueprintProtocol.Digest.to_tagged(evidence.deployment_digest),
  checks: checks,
  effective_bounds: match?({:ok, _}, BoundsAlgebra.BoundSet.to_map(evidence.effective_bounds)),
  clamps: Enum.map(evidence.clamps, &{&1.field, &1.requested, &1.effective}),
  optional_extensions_retained: evidence.optional_extensions_retained,
  not_verified: not_verified
}
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{
  protocol_revision: 1,
  checks: [
    {:canonical, ["blueprint"], true, :none},
    {:canonical, ["deployment"], true, :none},
    {:digest, ["blueprint"], true, :digest},
    {:digest, ["deployment"], true, :digest},
    {:negotiation, ["blueprint"], true, :none},
