## Run the shipped corpus

The corpus loader checks the installed files before the runner evaluates the cases. The report shows the agreement totals.

Load every shipped corpus file, run the cases, and build the aggregate report.

```elixir
alias AgentBlueprintProtocol.Conformance.{Corpus, Report, Runner}

corpus_root = Application.app_dir(:agent_blueprint_protocol, "priv/conformance")

corpus_files =
  corpus_root
  |> Path.join("**/*")
  |> Path.wildcard(match_dot: true)
  |> Enum.reject(&File.dir?/1)
  |> Map.new(fn path -> {Path.relative_to(path, corpus_root), File.read!(path)} end)

{:ok, corpus} = Corpus.load(corpus_files)
report = Report.build(corpus, Runner.run(corpus))

Map.take(report, [:agreement, :agreed, :disagreed, :total])
```

<!-- livebook:{"output":true} -->

```
%{total: 604, agreed: 604, agreement: true, disagreed: 0}
```

